description:
Does exact arithmetic and figure handling over the matter's verified figures, so no model ever computes or types a number. op "calc" runs fn (sum, diff, ratio, pct, product, date_add, date_diff, business_days) over operands that are verified finding values, written {"ref": "F12.v1"} exactly as ledger and extraction results show them, or literals with a unit ("21" with unit "days", "2026-11-12" with unit "date", "35" with unit "%"), and returns a worksheet with an id (wid) the deliverable can cite; every total, recalculated amount and computed date in the deliverable must be such a worksheet. product multiplies (a percentage counts as its fraction: 35% of a $612,400 shortfall); date_add and business_days take a negative count to count back from an event; date_add with holidays set (even []) rolls a result that lands on a weekend or one of those holidays to the next day that is not (backward for a negative count), as FRCP 6(a) does, and the worksheet shows the raw date. op "handles" gives each verified figure of fids (all when null) a codename such as {Zephyr} that keeps its figure for the whole run; drafters write the codename and the renderer substitutes the exact value. op "table" returns a Markdown key-figures table built only from verified values. Do not use it to estimate, round or infer a figure the record does not state, and do not use a quarantined finding's value: it is refused, never treated as zero.
Example: {"op": "calc", "fn": "product", "operands": [{"ref": "F3.v1", "literal": null, "unit": null}, {"ref": null, "literal": "35", "unit": "%"}], "holidays": null, "fids": null, "salientTop": null}
Example: {"op": "calc", "fn": "date_add", "operands": [{"ref": "F12.v1", "literal": null, "unit": null}, {"ref": null, "literal": "21", "unit": "days"}], "holidays": ["2026-11-11", "2026-11-26"], "fids": null, "salientTop": null}
Example: {"op": "handles", "fn": null, "operands": null, "holidays": null, "fids": null, "salientTop": 12}
